1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,440
This conflict began with but a single spark, and grew into a massive and terrible war.

2
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:14,920
The conflicting hopes and dreams of many different people have resulted in a great tragedy.

3
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:19,660
This is so sad and awful for everyone.

4
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:29,660
In addition to my grief at this war, I feel both shame and deep regret over our use of power for which...

5
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:43,540
Mankind was not ready, and so I hereby declare my succession to the Imperial Throne and take my place as Empress of the Verse Empire.

6
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:50,680
And also, I will be taking as my lawful husband, Count Cruteo of the Orbital Knights.

7
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:57,360
And as the Imperial Family of Verse, we wish to make peace with Earth.

8
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:06,800
In the name of the Empire of Verse, I command all Orbital Knights hearing these words, cease hostilities immediately!

9
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:13,140
What did she say? I thought that the plan was for Princess Asalem to found a new kingdom with Count Troyard.

10
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:14,780
But what about the U.F.E.?

11
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:19,520
We wait. Do nothing for now. Let's see which way the wind is blowing.

12
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:24,660
I should have known. After all, Troyard is nothing more than a lowborn Terran.

13
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,800
It's offensive to think of him in the Imperial Family.

14
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:29,460
What is this nonsense about?

15
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,240
Sir Harklight, return to base!

16
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:36,100
Lord Slain.

17
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:48,020
Why are they still shooting at us?

18
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:51,020
The Princess just ordered them all to stop fighting!

19
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,220
Now the Moonbase forces don't seem to want to stop.

20
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:57,600
Stay sharp! Heads up, everyone! We're not through with this battle!

21
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,140
Did you hear that?

22
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,500
Sure did.

23
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,360
That Princess Asalem just now.

24
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:08,440
Or rather, Empress Asalem. That was the princess that I remember.

25
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:09,400
You're right.

26
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:13,840
Everything Ensign Kaiska said to expect has come true.

27
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:17,160
That means that the ceasefire order was legitimate.

28
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:21,200
The enemies in front of us don't seem to feel like laying down their arms.

29
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,240
Are there any updates?

30
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,060
No, ma'am. Nothing at all. So it's follow last order.

31
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:29,060
Neither Moonbase nor Landing Castles show any sign of ceasing hostilities.

32
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:31,500
Current whereabouts of Empress Asalem?

33
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:36,360
Frequency analysis says it's originating from Count Mazurek's Landing Castle.

34
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:41,420
Has she abandoned the Moon? Or are we seeing a revolt?

35
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:46,020
Count Troyard, sir. What about Empress Asalem's order?

36
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:49,020
Order? I heard none.

37
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,600
Apologies, my lord.

38
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:56,720
What a surprise. Quite impressive of her.

39
00:02:56,720 --> 00:03:09,240
Princess Lemrina.

40
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:13,140
The Imperial Family's blood is what's crucial.

41
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:19,240
As long as you can activate Aldnoa, are you not still able to make your dream come true?

42
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:23,560
Know that I will not be going away.

43
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:33,400
This place has become the only one I can call home.

44
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:37,000
So please let me help you.

45
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,400
Of course.

46
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:44,160
Your kindness is deeply touching, Princess Lemrina.

47
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:48,100
Shall we, then?

48
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:52,720
Yes.

49
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,240
So pretty.

50
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,760
Was that terrible to say, seeing that?

51
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:12,060
Out there, there's terrible beauty all around.

52
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,020
I have seen such things.

53
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:16,220
Truly? Like what?

54
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:17,420
The future.

55
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:18,760
The future.

56
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:21,120
All of it. The good and the bad.

57
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:25,460
While my vision was limited only to the immediate future,

58
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:28,320
I thought that I could see everything.

59
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:31,960
Some was exactly as I foresaw.

60
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:33,900
However,

61
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:38,140
I failed to take into account

62
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:40,200
what was truly important.

63
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,000
Load and rearm.

64
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:49,420
Sir.

65
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,940
Lord Count Troyard!

66
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,160
What is the meaning of this?

67
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:56,480
What is Princess Asalem doing?

68
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:57,640
My lord slain.

69
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:01,460
I am issuing orders.

70
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:02,960
Patch this through command.

71
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,840
And include Stygia's squadron.

72
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:05,680
Yes, sir.

73
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,080
Attention!

74
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:12,100
Everyone evacuate the moon base immediately.

75
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,140
Begin your surrender,

76
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,860
including the landing castles.

77
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:19,900
We are abandoning the moon base!

78
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:21,820
Have you gone mad?

79
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:22,540
Slain!

80
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,640
Princess Lemrina,

81
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:28,480
for the many wrongs I have done you,

82
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:33,080
I sincerely apologize.

83
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:34,860
But Slain...

84
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,860
May you...

85
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:39,500
have a long and rich life.

86
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,240
Harklight,

87
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,660
please escort Princess Lemrina to a shuttle.

88
00:05:44,660 --> 00:05:46,160
Yes, sir.

89
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:46,740
As you wish.

90
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:47,260
No!

91
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:48,340
Slain!

92
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:49,860
Your Highness,

93
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,080
please come with me.

94
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:51,700
I won't go.

95
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:52,460
I won't.

96
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:53,400
Slain!

97
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,560
Slain!

98
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:57,680
Multiple signatures detected

99
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,680
leaving the moon base.

100
00:05:59,300 --> 00:05:59,860
Reinforcements?

101
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:01,440
No, Captain.

102
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:03,140
They're moving away

103
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:04,080
from the combat zone.

104
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:26,260
Thank you.

105
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:47,340
The Moonbase. It's blowing up. Did we do that?

106
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,520
Wasn't us.

107
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,480
Self-destruction?

108
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:57,960
Sir Harklyte!

109
00:06:58,380 --> 00:06:59,740
See to the shuttle's defense.

110
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:01,880
Sir Harklyte!

111
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:05,760
Harklyte, wait!

112
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:09,480
What are you doing? Turn back! Your orders were to surrender.

113
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:11,840
Harklyte!

114
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,520
Stigus Squadron! Combat is not authorized!

115
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:30,600
Enemy reinforcements, 10 o'clock. Minus 10 degrees angle of approach.

116
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,140
Stand by to engage.

117
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:36,180
Retreat! This is not a battle you can win. Don't throw your life away.

118
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,280
I made peace with death long ago.

119
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,320
Grant me this one selfish act.

120
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,340
Surrender right now! Harklyte!

121
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:46,120
I hope you can forgive me, my lord slain.

122
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:49,900
But I cannot comply with your order.

123
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:57,720
Can I come?

124
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,400
All units scattered!

125
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:18,400
Bastards!

126
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:18,920
Bastards!

127
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:27,760
How could they do this? Damn!

128
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:33,300
Wait a minute.

129
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,300
I know him.

130
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:46,900
Huh.

131
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:47,000
Huh.

132
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:53,220
You're absolutely correct, Harklyte.

133
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,880
We cannot allow it to end like this.

134
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,480
There is yet one thing

135
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:59,000
that I must do.

136
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:11,640
I've come for you, slain Troyard.

137
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:13,320
Let's settle matters now.

138
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,880
Hina ho, Kaisuka!

139
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,500
Oh, my God.

140
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:46,480
THE END

141
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:53,500
I THINK I KNOW THE ANSWER BUT I'LL ASK ANYWAY... WILL YOU SURRENDER, SLAY TROYARN?

142
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:57,500
YOU CAME ALL THIS WAY TO SAY SOMETHING SO POINTLESS, INAHO KAISKA?

143
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,500
NOT REALLY. I HAVE A DIFFERENT GOAL.

144
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:02,500
GLAD TO HEAR THAT... OR I'D BE DISAPPOINTED!

145
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:07,500
I THINK I KNOW THE ANSWER BUT I'LL ASK ANYWAY... WILL YOU SURRENDER, SLAY TROYARN?

146
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:10,500
I THINK I'M SURE YOU'RE NOT ABLE TO SAY SOMETHING SO POINTLESS, INAHO KAISKA?

147
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:12,500
NOT REALLY. I HAVE A DIFFERENT GOAL.

148
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:16,500
GLAD TO HEAR THAT... OR I'D BE DISAPPOINTED!

149
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:23,500
MY IMAGING SCREENS ARE GONE!

150
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:28,500
I GET IT. YOU CAN'T HANDLE ANY MORE HIGH-LOAD ANALYSIS.

151
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:31,500
TURN OFF PREDICTIVE IMAGERS.

152
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:35,500
I NO LONGER HAVE THE NEED FOR A FUTURE!

153
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:38,500
INCOMING! 2 O'CLOCK! ELEVATION 5 DEGREES!

154
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:41,500
COME ABOUT! ALL ENGINES FULL! HEADING 0-6-0!

155
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:43,500
AI-AI! COMING ABOUT!

156
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:46,500
LOAD CANISTER SHOT! FIRE WHEN YOU HAVE A LOCK!

157
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:07,500
NO WAY! ALL OF NOW'S COMBAT DATA IS AVAILABLE IN THE TACTICAL DATA LINK!

158
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,500
ALL UNITS REFER TO THAT-

159
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:15,500
YUKI! I'M OKAY!

160
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:23,500
ON BEHALF OF THE 37 CLAN'S ORBITAL KNIGHTS, I ASK YOU...

161
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,500
MIND IF I CUT IN?

162
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:28,500
WELCOME, COUNT BARO CRUZ.

163
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:34,500
INCOMING! 8 O'CLOCK! ELEVATION MINUS 25 DEGREES!

164
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,500
INTERCEPT THEM!

165
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:37,500
I'VE GOT THIS!

166
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,500
ONLY THREE ROUNDS LEFT!

167
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:07,500
IS-

168
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:08,500
INCOMING.

169
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,700
I WEARING

170
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:10,500
FIGHT WILL GAIN YOU NOTHING.

171
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,500
I AGREE...

172
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:13,500
BUT I HAVE NOTHING TO LOSE EITHER.

173
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,500
GIVING IN TO DESPAIR IS FOOLISH.

174
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,900
You just don't understand, do you?

175
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:20,180
This is the thing I desire the most!

176
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:31,780
Now you die!

177
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:37,460
Rai!

178
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:39,260
You fool!

179
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:51,500
Radar returns incoming!

180
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,500
Who?

181
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:55,500
My lord, it's the Tharsis and a UFE Cataphrat!

182
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,500
Those are...

183
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,500
Rai!

184
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:16,500
Three Direction Crossfire!

185
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,500
Target with multiple rounds!

186
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:19,500
Slay your fire control to me!

187
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:28,500
I hated it.

188
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:31,500
From when I first saw it, I hated it.

189
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,500
I hate that color!

190
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,500
Is that you, Sir Harklight?

191
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,500
The drones are all on autopilot!

192
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:48,500
Get behind the boulders!

193
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,500
We can limit the direction of their attack!

194
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:51,500
Attack!

195
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:56,500
Are you alright?

196
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:57,500
Mostly.

197
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,500
But I did lose one of my arms.

198
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:01,500
Sir Harklight!

199
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:02,500
Battle status?

200
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:07,500
Including myself, there are three Stygis Masters remaining with only six slave units.

201
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,500
The rest were taken down by the UFE.

202
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:12,500
I've used up most of my ammunition.

203
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:14,500
And you, Count Boracruz?

204
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:17,500
The right arm on Octantis is non-functional.

205
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:20,500
It must have been damaged during that last attack.

206
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:25,500
It seems Terran warriors are not without skill.

207
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,500
True.

208
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:31,500
It is, after all, where Lord Slane was born.

209
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:36,500
Yes, it is much like fighting a great sandstorm on Olympus.

210
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:40,500
It seems we may have misread the winds.

211
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:41,500
Let's do this.

212
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:43,500
I'm with you.

213
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:45,500
Enemy formation, nine o'clock!

214
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:47,500
Twenty degrees elevation!

215
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:48,500
All guns, lock on!

216
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:50,500
Cataphract platoon!

217
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,500
All units, fire at will!

218
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,500
Hmm.

219
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:14,500
All act as a drogue chute.

220
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,500
That will stabilize you.

221
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,500
Do you intend to die too?

222
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:20,500
You'll burn up.

223
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,500
Cataphract frames are very high density.

224
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:25,500
It should work as an ablation shield.

225
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:27,500
Impossible.

226
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:28,500
It can't be done.

227
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:30,500
Really?

228
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:31,500
Guess we'll see.

229
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:37,500
Sis, look!

230
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,500
There!

231
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,500
A shooting star.

232
00:15:57,500 --> 00:16:18,660
That might be

233
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:21,500
Under the mountain helen in the desert.

234
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:49,960
And there it is.

235
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:56,960
Aldnoa Reactor 1, constructed as a sign of goodwill between Earth and Verse, is scheduled to be activated today.

236
00:16:56,960 --> 00:17:02,960
We're told that Empress of Salem herself will take part in this inaugural activation ceremony.

237
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:08,960
Research is continuing into opening up the activation ability and privileges to everyone.

238
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:15,960
Once that is achieved, industrial use of Aldnoa will rapidly develop and help greatly with Earth's reconstruction.

239
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:21,960
As the sole provider of Aldnoa, it should also generate much needed capital for the Verse Empire.

240
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:27,960
The activation theories of Dr. Troyard have already been proven, so we should be seeing great progress.

241
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:39,960
That's true. Yet it is darkly ironic that slain Troyard, son of that same Dr. Troyard, plotted the assassination of Empress of Salem, which was the trigger for the second interplanetary war.

242
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:45,960
Yes, but the death of slain Troyard was the event which allowed Earth and Verse to enact a friendship treaty.

243
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:49,960
Correct. But there are still Mars Knights occupying Earth territory.

244
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:54,960
One goal of Empress of Salem's visit is peace negotiations with those Knights.

245
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:58,960
Here's hoping that we will see the prompt return of that territory.

246
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:07,960
In the clear hope that the light we create here will be a bridge of peace between Earth and Verse.

247
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:11,960
Awaken!

248
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:24,960
Thank you.

249
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:28,960
Feeling well?

250
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:33,960
You don't look that bad.

251
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:36,960
You could do a better job of eating your food, though.

252
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:41,960
The warden is getting concerned.

253
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:45,960
It's your move.

254
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:46,960
Your eye?

255
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:47,960
Hm?

256
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,960
Is that from when I shot you?

257
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:52,960
Analytical engine.

258
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,960
I had a bio device implanted in there.

259
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,960
It was neural linked to my cranial nerves.

260
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,960
But I had it removed.

261
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,960
Don't need it now.

262
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,960
Let me die.

263
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:05,960
I deceived.

264
